{
  "scenarioId": "neo-rendezvous",
  "scenarioVersion": "0.1.0",
  "title": "Echoes of Origins",
  "referenceEarthRangeM": 37399000000.0,
  "narrative": "Send a small spacecraft to rendezvous with a near-Earth asteroid and decide what its surface can tell us about the early Solar System.",
  "topConstraints": [
    "Keep launch mass under the dedicated small-lift limit (300 kg) with margin.",
    "Return every observation the instruments generate: downlinked data must keep up with generated data.",
    "Stay within the 60 M USD mission budget."
  ],
  "fidelityNotes": [
    "All catalogue values are illustrative gameplay-estimate archetypes, not real hardware.",
    "Trajectory: scenario-preset. Departure and arrival dates, C3 (14 km2/s2), departure and arrival V-infinity and mission delta-v (0.25 km/s) are illustrative gameplay values; a JPL-derived option replaces the preset in Phase 5.",
    "Destination: synthetic target 'Scenario target NEO-A (illustrative)'; it is not a real asteroid.",
    "Starter design deliberately pairs the high-data-rate camera with the low-gain X-band radio, so generated data exceeds downlink capacity: swapping to comms-xband-medium (or cutting the camera duty cycle) clears the data-buffer warning.",
    "Reference Earth-spacecraft range for the link budget is 0.25 AU (3.74e10 m): an illustrative mid-mission Earth-NEO distance chosen for gameplay, not an ephemeris value. Ground segment is ground-large (62 dBi, 40 K, 0.33 contact availability). Link budget (arch 7.5 equation, 8.4 GHz, 0.25 AU): comms-xband-medium closes the planned 50 kbit/s downlink with margin above 3 dB; comms-xband-lowgain does not close it.",
    "The starter warning is a data-return shortfall (downlink capacity): generated data exceeds what the low-gain radio can return, while onboard storage is not the limiting factor.",
    "Downlink plan rates are the planned rate; the achievable rate is capped by the selected radio's maximum data rate.",
    "Optional extra objectives (thermal behaviour, magnetic/plasma environment) are listed in optionalObjectives and are not part of the starter MissionState.",
    "Measurement targetThreshold values are the scheduled observation time each requirement needs (seconds, gameplay-estimate); the starter plan schedules slightly more than required, so the only starter shortfall is data return.",
    "The shape-model requirement still targets about 2 m resolution (illustrative); its targetThreshold field carries the scheduled observation time the engine checks, not the resolution."
  ],
  "optionalObjectives": [
    {
      "id": "obj-thermal",
      "title": "Thermal behaviour",
      "question": "How does the surface heat and cool across the asteroid day?",
      "priority": 1.0,
      "requiredMeasurements": [
        {
          "id": "meas-thermal-ir",
          "description": "Surface thermal-infrared radiometry across a rotation",
          "instrumentCapability": "thermal-infrared",
          "coverageWeight": 1.0,
          "required": true
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obj-magnetic",
      "title": "Magnetic and plasma environment",
      "question": "Does the asteroid carry a remanent magnetic field?",
      "priority": 0.5,
      "requiredMeasurements": [
        {
          "id": "meas-magnetometry",
          "description": "Magnetic field survey during close approach",
          "instrumentCapability": "magnetometry",
          "coverageWeight": 1.0,
          "required": false
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
